From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:50:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/75] Do not keep the hidden high parameter in a register
 when a nested routine uses it (#41289)

A nested routine that assigns to the outer routine's open string
parameter loads the hidden high parameter during its own firstpass, after
the parent's code was generated with that parameter in a register:
Internal error 200409241 (tests/webtbs/tw41282 at -O2 and up, -OoREGVAR).
Mark the high parameter not regable together with the parameter accessed
from the nested routine. Old defect; Delphi mode exposes it since open
strings became the default there.
---
 compiler/nld.pas | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/nld.pas b/compiler/nld.pas
index eff75707..ea02d267 100644
--- a/compiler/nld.pas
+++ b/compiler/nld.pas
@@ -362,6 +362,8 @@ implementation
 
 
     function tloadnode.pass_typecheck:tnode;
+      var
+        highsym : tabstractvarsym;
       begin
          result:=nil;
          case symtableentry.typ of
@@ -414,6 +416,20 @@ implementation
                    { reference in nested procedures, variable needs to be in memory }
                    { and behaves as if its address escapes its parent block         }
                    make_not_regable(self,[ra_different_scope]);
+                   { the same goes for the hidden high parameter of an open array or
+                     open string parameter: the nested routine may first load it
+                     during its firstpass (e.g. when assigning to an open string),
+                     but the parent's code, which decides where the high parameter
+                     lives, has already been generated by then (tw41282, #41289) }
+                   if symtableentry.typ=paravarsym then
+                     begin
+                       highsym:=get_high_value_sym(tparavarsym(symtableentry));
+                       if assigned(highsym) then
+                         begin
+                           highsym.different_scope:=true;
+                           highsym.varregable:=vr_none;
+                         end;
+                     end;
                  end
                { if this is a nested function and it uses the Self parameter then
                  consider this as captured as well (needed for anonymous functions) }
